      "rev_n_4_43cd8e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_43cd8e_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_43cd8e",
        "thought_text": "To correctly identify the repeating part of the decimal and convert it to a fraction, we need to use the formula for repeating decimals: numerator = repeating_int - non_repeating_int * (10^repeat_count - 1) // (10^repeat_count - 1), where repeating_int is the integer value of the repeating part, and non_repeating_int is the integer value of the non-repeating part. This formula accounts for the place value of the repeating digits and ensures we get the correct fraction representation.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6994478952353875872",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_43cd8e_0",
